# Privacy Policy for Lucca A53 Mini

**Effective Date:** May 26, 2026

## 1. Introduction
This Privacy Policy applies to the Lucca A53 Mini Android application ("App"), which operates as an S1 Timer Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) Controller[cite: 1, 4]. We respect your privacy and are committed to protecting it. This document outlines our data practices and clearly explains how the App interacts with your device.

## 2. Data Collection and Use
**We do not collect, store, use, transmit, share, or sell any personal information or user data.** 

The App operates entirely locally on your Android device to communicate directly with your S1 hardware[cite: 1, 4]. We do not utilize user accounts, remote servers, analytics software, crash reporting tools, or any background tracking mechanisms. Everything you do within the App stays on your phone and the connected S1 device.

## 3. Required Permissions and Local Data
To function correctly, the App requires specific Android permissions to discover and connect to your S1 Timer hardware[cite: 1, 4]. 

*   **Bluetooth Permissions (`BLUETOOTH_SCAN`, `BLUETOOTH_CONNECT`):** Required to scan for and establish a connection with the S1 Timer's custom Bluetooth service[cite: 1].
*   **Location Permissions (`ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION`):** Required by the Android operating system on older API levels to enable Bluetooth scanning[cite: 1]. 

**Important Clarification:** These permissions are used *strictly* for local device-to-device Bluetooth communication. At no point does the App record your physical location, track your movements, or transmit your Bluetooth data to the developer or any third party.

## 4. Third-Party Services
The App does not integrate with any third-party services, tracking APIs, advertising networks, or external cloud servers. 

## 5. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in Android OS requirements or App updates. If any changes are made, we will update the "Effective Date" at the top of this document. However, our core commitment to collecting zero personal information will remain unchanged.

